1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,540
This is MaintOps: an AI assistant that finds the right handyman for a household problem, and runs the job from the first report to the final review. It's built end to end on Databricks.

2
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:20,189
A client simply describes the problem to Manny, our agent. Manny classifies it, logs an incident in Lakebase, and searches for the best handymen.

3
00:00:20,739 --> 00:00:37,326
The ranking is deterministic code, not the language model: skill match, success on similar jobs from the Spark pipeline, reviews, workload, and real travel time from Geoapify, by car or by public transport. Every figure Manny states is checked against the data.

4
00:00:37,876 --> 00:00:43,020
The client picks one and confirms, and the dashboard updates in place, without a reload.

5
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:51,512
The handyman taps I'm on my way, from home, the last job or another address, and the client immediately sees the expected arrival.

6
00:00:52,062 --> 00:01:02,940
To complete a job, Manny asks for the hours worked and the amount paid, repeats them, and saves only after an explicit yes. These figures keep each handyman's hourly rate up to date.

7
00:01:03,490 --> 00:01:09,187
Handymen can also ask about their reviews, and get the recurring pattern plus one practical tip.

8
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:18,300
New handymen sign up with a CV. ai parse document reads the PDF, Manny extracts the profile and address, and geocoding adds the region.

9
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:28,482
Under the hood, Lakebase holds the live state. Its change data feed streams into Delta, where a Spark streaming job refreshes the affected scorecards in under a minute.

10
00:01:29,032 --> 00:01:43,375
A batch pipeline takes a one-million-incident history through eighteen validation rules into scorecards, and a Declarative Pipeline turns every agent request and tool call into analytics. A burst of a thousand reviews was reflected in thirty-seven seconds.

11
00:01:43,925 --> 00:01:58,922
And no version of Manny reaches users without passing a release gate: 71 multi-turn scenarios, three runs each, and about two thousand checks written in code. It has stopped real mistakes, like an invented emergency number, before they shipped.

12
00:01:59,472 --> 00:02:05,664
The code, the measurements behind every claim, and the live app are all linked in the README. Thanks for watching.
